<title>UK: Ex-dividends take 4.309 points off UK's FTSE index.</title>
<headline>Ex-dividends take 4.309 points off UK's FTSE index.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>FTSE International said the following FTSE-100 stocks will go ex-dividend on Tuesday and the effect will be to take 4.309 points off the index at the start of trading.</p>
<p>					 DIVIDEND	INDEX</p>
<p>					 (PENCE)	 EFFECT</p>
<p>		 COMPANY	     Net   Gross    Gross</p>
<p>     * Cable &amp; Wireless	  7.70   9.625    1.259</p>
<p>     * Marks &amp; Spencer	   9.70  12.125    2.007</p>
<p>     * Next			 10.00  12.500    0.273</p>
<p>     * Safeway		     9.70  12.125    0.770</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
